+        """Adopt a window grant SMALLER than the one this agent is running at —
+        but only while the resident prompt still fits under the smaller trigger.
+        Returns the (possibly lowered) window. Never raises. [bd-dre-x3n0x]
+
+        ⛔ WHY THIS EXISTS. The broker publishes a share-bounded ``main_window``
+        per session, and until now NOTHING READ IT — it was an inert number, so
+        the only bound that bit was ``main_grow_max`` (stop growing). That leaves
+        the recurrence hole that caused the 2026-09-30 deadlock to be reachable
+        with no growth at all: two architect mains launch at the profile's
+        configured 393,216 window, whose compaction triggers are 327,270 each,
+        and 2 x 335,462 = 670,924 in-flight tokens against a 406,138-token usable
+        pool. Both sessions simply ride up to their triggers and the pool wedges.
+
+        ⛔ WHY IT NEVER SHRINKS A SESSION THAT IS ALREADY FULL. Andre 2026-09-30:
+        a live session's context is his call, not the broker's. So the grant is
+        adopted only when ``footprint(granted) > current prompt`` — i.e. when
+        lowering the window does NOT force a compaction this turn. A fresh main
+        with a 30K prompt therefore settles onto its share immediately; the
+        grandfathered 433K session is left exactly alone and is instead denied
+        growth (it appears in invariant.grants.grandfathered, and only a relaunch
+        brings its held context down).
+
+        Opt out with HERMES_POOL_SHRINK=0.
+        """
+        import os          # module-level `os` is not in this file's namespace
+
+        try:
+            if role != "main" or os.environ.get("HERMES_POOL_SHRINK", "1") == "0":
+                return cur
+            granted = int(sess.get("main_window") or 0)
+            if not granted or granted >= cur:
